 protective equipment people want to  know how we get out of lockdown labour  pushing too  here the plan will the Primus to give  that reassurance by setting out his plan  as he says he will or will he come to  this house or Monday to present that  plan we want if we possibly can to get  going with some of these measures on  Monday I think it will be a good thing  mr. speaker if if people had an idea of  what's coming the Prime Minister wants  to tweak the lock down as early as  Monday well what might that look like a  senior minister tells me that could mean  reopening smaller shops and outdoor  workplaces but they are still looking at  the data the watchword in all of this is  caution stamping on the accelerator just  too dangerous think of this more as  slowly lifting your foot off the brake  the PM wants to lift the lockdown  nationally but devising a road map to  navigate a disease you still don't fully  understand is difficult the government  desperate to avoid a second peak but  expect bumps along the road beth Rigby  Sky News Westminster
 

